---
title: 'Fills & Borders'
---

This section describes how to change the fills and borders of various parts of the chart.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Fills & Borders" name="fills-borders" type="generated" /%}

In the example above:

-   A border is drawn around the series area with a corner radius and no padding.
-   A border, fill and corner radius are applied to the legend, with padding between the border and items as a single number.
-   A border, fill and corner radius are applied to the series data labels with padding defined for each of the top, right, bottom and left.

## Fills

See [Series Fills](./fills) for details on customising the fills for each series.

## Padding

The padding can be provided as either a single number of an object with values for `top`, `right`, `bottom` and `left`.

